From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukas Rieger <lukas@local>
Date: Fri, 21 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] diag: Forward unregistered subsystem commands to modem

On APQ/wearable platforms (e.g. SDA429W) the modem does not register
certain DIAG subsystem commands (notably EFS2 / subsystem 0x13) in the
AP-side routing table, even though the modem firmware handles them.

Without this patch, unregistered subsystem dispatch commands are
rejected with DIAG_BAD_CMD_F (0x15) instead of being forwarded to the
modem.  This prevents userspace tools from accessing the modem's EFS
filesystem to provision NV items such as gnss_external_lna_state.

Add a fallback before the error response that forwards any unregistered
subsystem dispatch command (cmd_code 0x4B) to the modem peripheral
when it is online.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [device-specific workaround]
Signed-off-by: Lukas Rieger <lukas@local>
---
 drivers/char/diag/diagfwd.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/char/diag/diagfwd.c b/drivers/char/diag/diagfwd.c
index fda283fcb7a3..7f1a45223c7b 100644
--- a/drivers/char/diag/diagfwd.c
+++ b/drivers/char/diag/diagfwd.c
@@ -1344,6 +1344,22 @@ int diag_process_apps_pkt(unsigned char *buf, int len, int pid)
 #endif

 	/* We have now come to the end of the function. */
+	/*
+	 * Forward unregistered subsystem commands to the modem if it is
+	 * online.  On APQ/wearable platforms the modem may not register
+	 * certain subsystems (e.g. EFS2 / 0x13) even though its firmware
+	 * handles them.  Without this fallback those commands are silently
+	 * rejected with DIAG_BAD_CMD_F.
+	 */
+	if (len >= 4 && *buf == DIAG_CMD_DIAG_SUBSYS &&
+	    driver->diagfwd_cntl[PERIPHERAL_MODEM] &&
+	    driver->diagfwd_cntl[PERIPHERAL_MODEM]->ch_open) {
+		int fwd_err = diagfwd_write(PERIPHERAL_MODEM, TYPE_CMD,
+					    buf, len);
+		if (fwd_err == 0)
+			return 0;
+	}
+
 	if (chk_apps_only())
 		diag_send_error_rsp(buf, len, pid);

